1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,679
Welcome to PulseTwin, a personal blood pressure digital twin prepared for Team Gimites.

2
00:00:06,679 --> 00:00:14,899
The team leader is Yashwanth M, joined by Kalashikam Vijay Krishna, Subiksha K, and Shakthi K.

3
00:00:14,899 --> 00:00:20,551
This version adds ten research features to a working, interpretable prototype.

4
00:00:20,551 --> 00:00:30,826
We will explore scenario comparisons, saved settings, daily observations, data quality, trends, sensitivity, errors, uncertainty, shareable hypotheses, and printable evidence.

5
00:00:30,826 --> 00:00:39,047
The central idea remains simple: daily observations should help us ask better questions about possible futures.

6
00:00:39,047 --> 00:00:46,240
Every example uses synthetic data, and no clinical accuracy or treatment benefit is claimed.

7
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:51,377
This voiceover is synthesized, with captures from the running application.

8
00:00:51,377 --> 00:01:01,653
The code, architecture, model card, tests, and presentation are included so reviewers can reproduce the walkthrough and inspect its assumptions.

9
00:01:04,153 --> 00:01:12,389
Imagine a person with three months of blood pressure readings, step counts, sleep notes, dietary estimates, and self-reported stress.

10
00:01:12,389 --> 00:01:20,625
A conventional chart can show a trend, but it cannot explain how these measurements fit together for that individual.

11
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:25,826
A generic wellness score often hides the relationship behind a single number.

12
00:01:25,826 --> 00:01:36,663
PulseTwin explores a different interaction: make the personal model visible, let the user specify a hypothetical scenario, and show the uncertainty next to the result.

13
00:01:36,663 --> 00:01:42,298
This is a research problem rather than a promise to lower blood pressure.

14
00:01:42,298 --> 00:01:48,367
Many important drivers are unmeasured, and lifestyle variables can be correlated with each other.

15
00:01:48,367 --> 00:01:52,701
Our design treats those limitations as part of the product.

16
00:01:52,701 --> 00:01:58,770
The goal is to support informed questions, not to turn observational patterns into prescriptions.

17
00:02:01,270 --> 00:02:10,355
The selected use case is longitudinal cardiometabolic research and education, with systolic blood pressure as the single modeled outcome.

18
00:02:10,355 --> 00:02:20,397
A researcher or an authorized user can inspect how a person's observations relate to daily habits and explore a conditional future.

19
00:02:20,397 --> 00:02:27,569
We deliberately avoid a broad health score, disease diagnosis, medication recommendations, and automated clinical decisions.

20
00:02:27,569 --> 00:02:34,742
A narrow outcome makes the model easier to inspect and the prototype easier to validate.

21
00:02:34,742 --> 00:02:42,871
The application does not contain a physician workflow, electronic health record integration, or a live wearable connection.

22
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:47,653
Those are possible future integrations, not features we claim today.

23
00:02:47,653 --> 00:02:55,782
The complete implemented loop is observation ingestion, validation, personal fitting, residual state updating, scenario simulation, and review.

24
00:02:55,782 --> 00:03:01,041
Keeping this scope explicit is essential to evaluating the submission fairly.

25
00:03:03,541 --> 00:03:05,691
Here is the running dashboard.

26
00:03:05,691 --> 00:03:11,711
The active profile is Asha, a fictional label attached to a deterministic synthetic dataset.

27
00:03:11,711 --> 00:03:16,010
The profile bar states the observation count and date range.

28
00:03:16,010 --> 00:03:25,039
Across the top, three cards separate current modeled systolic pressure, the chosen scenario at the selected horizon, and held-out prediction error.

29
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:34,498
The current number is a model estimate at the most recent seven-day average habits; it is not simply the last cuff reading.

30
00:03:34,498 --> 00:03:38,798
The scenario number depends on the controls at the right.

31
00:03:38,798 --> 00:03:42,237
Prediction error comes from a separate chronological evaluation.

32
00:03:42,237 --> 00:03:50,836
Keeping these three concepts distinct prevents a future scenario from being mistaken for a measured reading or an accuracy guarantee.

33
00:03:50,836 --> 00:03:55,566
Notice also the persistent research notice and the synthetic data badge.

34
00:03:55,566 --> 00:03:59,005
These disclosures remain part of the normal workflow.

35
00:04:01,505 --> 00:04:05,719
The first two new tools strengthen the observation loop.

36
00:04:05,719 --> 00:04:10,402
The daily update form selects the next consecutive date automatically.

37
00:04:10,402 --> 00:04:15,552
Enter a systolic reading and daily habits, then add the observation.

38
00:04:15,552 --> 00:04:22,107
The server validates the complete sequence before the new history replaces the active session.

39
00:04:22,107 --> 00:04:30,067
The model is refitted, and the interface shows the modeled current pressure before and after the update.

40
00:04:30,067 --> 00:04:36,154
Updated observations remain selectable during the session and can be exported as CSV.

41
00:04:36,154 --> 00:04:43,646
Alongside this, data-quality review identifies unusual readings, large daily changes, constant predictors, and highly correlated inputs.

42
00:04:43,646 --> 00:04:47,860
These are transparent engineering heuristics rather than clinical thresholds.

43
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:51,606
They never silently remove or repair a row.

44
00:04:51,606 --> 00:04:55,352
A clean review is not a medical certification.

45
00:04:55,352 --> 00:05:02,375
The purpose is to expose measurement context and weakly identified associations before interpreting a scenario.

46
00:05:04,875 --> 00:05:08,618
The first modeling layer is Bayesian linear regression.

47
00:05:08,618 --> 00:05:13,296
Four standardized habit features and an intercept describe systolic pressure.

48
00:05:13,296 --> 00:05:16,103
Each person gets a separate fit.

49
00:05:16,103 --> 00:05:22,185
There is no pretrained neural network, external language model, or hidden population dataset.

50
00:05:22,185 --> 00:05:30,606
Gaussian priors regularize the coefficients so a small or correlated history does not lead to an unconstrained fit.

51
00:05:30,606 --> 00:05:36,220
The posterior mean and covariance are calculated directly using NumPy matrix operations.

52
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:43,238
The prior values are illustrative engineering choices, not clinical effect sizes copied from a trial.

53
00:05:43,238 --> 00:05:51,659
In particular, the model does not prove that increasing one habit will cause a particular change in pressure.

54
00:05:51,659 --> 00:05:55,870
It estimates an association conditional on the recorded inputs.

55
00:05:55,870 --> 00:06:04,291
The repository contains the exact feature scales, prior values, equations, noise assumptions, and limitations in the model card.

56
00:06:06,791 --> 00:06:12,889
A static regression alone would not capture the concept of an updating twin.

57
00:06:12,889 --> 00:06:19,457
PulseTwin adds a scalar Kalman filter over the residual pressure after the regression prediction.

58
00:06:19,457 --> 00:06:26,024
This state represents slow unobserved drift without naming it as a specific disease mechanism.

59
00:06:26,024 --> 00:06:34,937
Each daily residual adjusts the current state using a Kalman gain, while process variance expresses additional uncertainty over time.

60
00:06:34,937 --> 00:06:43,381
When a new history is imported, the personal coefficients are refitted and the residual sequence is filtered again.

61
00:06:43,381 --> 00:06:49,011
This is a two-stage approximation, not a joint physiological state-space inference system.

62
00:06:49,011 --> 00:06:54,171
The covariance does not capture every dependency between coefficients and state.

63
00:06:54,171 --> 00:06:57,924
The implementation is a human-in-the-loop, data-driven twin prototype.

64
00:06:57,924 --> 00:07:06,837
It provides a repeatable observation and simulation loop, while continuous sensor synchronization and clinical feedback are explicitly future work.

65
00:07:09,337 --> 00:07:19,143
The scenario comparison tool lets a reviewer pin the current settings as a reference, change the controls, and simulate a second possibility.

66
00:07:19,143 --> 00:07:24,937
Both curves are recomputed against the same active observations, horizon, and interval level.

67
00:07:24,937 --> 00:07:31,623
Switching profiles recalculates the reference rather than carrying an old person's prediction into the comparison.

68
00:07:31,623 --> 00:07:38,309
The displayed endpoint difference is a difference of conditional means, not an estimated treatment effect.

69
00:07:38,309 --> 00:07:44,103
The adjacent library saves up to eight named settings in the current browser.

70
00:07:44,103 --> 00:07:49,898
An entry contains a generic label, four hypothetical inputs, horizon, and interval level.

71
00:07:49,898 --> 00:07:54,801
It does not contain observation records, profile identity, or fitted results.

72
00:07:54,801 --> 00:08:01,932
Load an entry to apply it to the current history, or delete it from the library.

73
00:08:01,932 --> 00:08:06,835
This makes repeated experimentation convenient while keeping the data boundary clear.

74
00:08:09,335 --> 00:08:15,752
The uncertainty lens now supports eighty, ninety, ninety-five, and ninety-nine percent predictive intervals.

75
00:08:15,752 --> 00:08:19,207
Select a level in the scenario studio.

76
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:25,130
The forecast band, legend, exported report, and held-out coverage all update consistently.

77
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:28,585
The model's predicted mean does not change.

78
00:08:28,585 --> 00:08:39,444
A wider band is not evidence that the model became more accurate; it expresses a different coverage statement under the same assumptions.

79
00:08:39,444 --> 00:08:47,341
The band combines coefficient uncertainty, residual-state uncertainty, fixed observation noise, and process variance over the horizon.

80
00:08:47,341 --> 00:08:55,239
It still does not capture every source of confounding, measurement bias, changing medication, or model misspecification.

81
00:08:55,239 --> 00:09:00,668
The uncertainty panel states the endpoint interval and its width explicitly.

82
00:09:00,668 --> 00:09:07,085
Tests verify that interval widths expand with confidence while the mean stays fixed.

83
00:09:07,085 --> 00:09:13,008
This makes the uncertainty control meaningful rather than a cosmetic chart setting.

84
00:09:15,508 --> 00:09:21,371
The sensitivity explorer asks a narrower question than changing four controls together.

85
00:09:21,371 --> 00:09:24,303
Choose movement, sleep, sodium, or stress.

86
00:09:24,303 --> 00:09:32,610
The model evaluates seven target values for that one input while holding the other scenario settings fixed.

87
00:09:32,610 --> 00:09:37,985
The curve shows the projected systolic pressure at the current horizon.

88
00:09:37,985 --> 00:09:44,337
The sweep stays within the intersection of observed values and permitted scenario bounds.

89
00:09:44,337 --> 00:09:51,178
If that intersection is empty, the application reports that no valid sweep is available.

90
00:09:51,178 --> 00:09:56,553
The personal coefficient and its ninety-five percent interval are also shown.

91
00:09:56,553 --> 00:10:04,372
This coefficient interval is labeled separately from the selectable predictive interval, because they describe different quantities.

92
00:10:04,372 --> 00:10:08,769
Correlated or constant inputs can make coefficients poorly identified.

93
00:10:08,769 --> 00:10:14,633
The sensitivity curve is therefore an inspectable association, not a recommended intervention.

94
00:10:14,633 --> 00:10:19,031
Automated checks compare sweep outputs against direct scenario simulations.

95
00:10:21,531 --> 00:10:26,423
Two additional panels show information that a single accuracy number hides.

96
00:10:26,423 --> 00:10:36,206
Longitudinal trends plot the seven-day rolling mean and summarize the latest week's pressure, its change from the previous week, and recent variability.

97
00:10:36,206 --> 00:10:42,432
A recent linear slope is descriptive history, not an attributed cause or a forecast.

98
00:10:42,432 --> 00:10:47,768
Error diagnostics show each held-out observation beside its prediction and signed residual.

99
00:10:47,768 --> 00:10:51,326
Positive bias means the model tends to underpredict.

100
00:10:51,326 --> 00:10:59,775
Root mean squared error highlights larger misses, while maximum absolute error exposes the worst miss in the small holdout.

101
00:10:59,775 --> 00:11:04,222
The evaluation still fits only on the chronological training prefix.

102
00:11:04,222 --> 00:11:09,113
Held-out pressure labels do not enter the fit or state update.

103
00:11:09,113 --> 00:11:14,005
Held-out daily habits are known inputs, so this remains conditional prediction.

104
00:11:14,005 --> 00:11:19,341
These panels make both the history and model failures easier to question.

105
00:11:21,841 --> 00:11:36,249
On the included synthetic fixtures, Asha has a twin mean absolute error of three point zero one millimeters of mercury, Dev has three point one nine, and Mira has two point eight one.

106
00:11:36,249 --> 00:11:44,982
The training-mean baselines have errors of three point six zero, three point eight five, and four point four seven respectively.

107
00:11:44,982 --> 00:11:48,474
The last-reading baselines are weaker on these fixtures.

108
00:11:48,474 --> 00:11:53,714
All fourteen held-out readings fall within the predictive interval for each profile.

109
00:11:53,714 --> 00:12:02,009
That does not establish reliable calibration, because fourteen examples are a tiny sample and the bands may be conservative.

110
00:12:02,009 --> 00:12:08,122
More importantly, the synthetic generator uses approximately linear relationships similar to the fitted model.

111
00:12:08,122 --> 00:12:12,924
These results demonstrate that the implementation behaves sensibly on its fixtures.

112
00:12:12,924 --> 00:12:19,037
They are not evidence of clinical accuracy, causal benefit, or generalization to real patients.

113
00:12:21,537 --> 00:12:30,059
The shareable-settings action creates a URL containing only the hypothetical inputs, horizon, interval level, and a schema version.

114
00:12:30,059 --> 00:12:33,847
It excludes observation history, profile identity, and predictions.

115
00:12:33,847 --> 00:12:38,581
A recipient applies those settings to their own active data.

116
00:12:38,581 --> 00:12:47,577
The application validates the values and rejects malformed links, including when a link is opened in the same tab.

117
00:12:47,577 --> 00:12:56,573
A local address still requires an accessible application instance; this is not a claim of a publicly hosted demo.

118
00:12:56,573 --> 00:13:00,361
The printable report provides a second handoff path.

119
00:13:00,361 --> 00:13:12,671
It collects the current model version, data provenance, observation period, scenario assumptions, predicted endpoint, interval, holdout metrics, review flags, and limitations in a clean PDF-ready layout.

120
00:13:12,671 --> 00:13:17,879
Unlike the settings link, a report may identify its active profile.

121
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:21,667
The user should share it only with authorization.

122
00:13:24,167 --> 00:13:27,929
The implementation has a deliberately small architecture.

123
00:13:27,929 --> 00:13:32,229
A static browser application handles interaction and visualization.

124
00:13:32,229 --> 00:13:39,753
FastAPI serves the interface and exposes health, synthetic profile, CSV import, and analysis endpoints.

125
00:13:39,753 --> 00:13:43,515
Pydantic validates JSON and parsed CSV observations.

126
00:13:43,515 --> 00:13:49,427
NumPy computes the Bayesian fit, filtered state, scenario, and chronological evaluation.

127
00:13:49,427 --> 00:13:56,414
The server returns a structured report, which the browser renders and can download.

128
00:13:56,414 --> 00:14:03,401
There is no database, analytics service, external model provider, or paid API dependency.

129
00:14:03,401 --> 00:14:08,776
After package installation, the application works without external network calls.

130
00:14:08,776 --> 00:14:15,225
The architecture document shows both the request flow and the trust boundary.

131
00:14:15,225 --> 00:14:23,825
This simplicity makes the prototype easy to inspect and run, but it is not production security.

132
00:14:23,825 --> 00:14:32,424
Authentication, secure deployment, retention controls, and clinical governance would be required before handling real patient workflows.

133
00:14:34,924 --> 00:14:39,975
The repository now includes twenty-four automated model and API tests.

134
00:14:39,975 --> 00:14:52,604
New checks verify that confidence levels change widths without changing means, known linear histories produce the expected trends, and quality flags do not remove observations.

135
00:14:52,604 --> 00:15:03,211
Constant and correlated predictors, empty sensitivity ranges, exact residual metrics, and parity between sensitivity curves and direct simulations are also covered.

136
00:15:03,211 --> 00:15:09,778
The daily update test confirms that an additional observation changes the personal model.

137
00:15:09,778 --> 00:15:17,355
Browser acceptance uses real Chromium to exercise all ten new workflows and the original dashboard.

138
00:15:17,355 --> 00:15:30,489
It verifies saved settings survive reload, deletion works, shared links omit observations, invalid links are rejected, session updates retain provenance, and a printable PDF is produced.

139
00:15:30,489 --> 00:15:35,035
Mobile overflow and JavaScript errors are checked as well.

140
00:15:35,035 --> 00:15:38,571
These are engineering tests, not clinical validation.

141
00:15:41,071 --> 00:15:46,308
PulseTwin includes three deterministic synthetic profiles and no patient records.

142
00:15:46,308 --> 00:15:52,592
The application has no server-side persistence and makes no external AI calls.

143
00:15:52,592 --> 00:16:01,495
Uploaded observations travel to the local API and remain in request memory and the active browser session.

144
00:16:01,495 --> 00:16:08,827
A downloaded report contains its underlying observations, so exporting is a deliberate data-handling action.

145
00:16:08,827 --> 00:16:19,301
The prototype does not have user authentication, clinical access controls, or production hardening, and it should remain local during evaluation.

146
00:16:19,301 --> 00:16:26,109
Model warnings explain observational uncertainty and identify scenarios beyond the observed input range.

147
00:16:26,109 --> 00:16:32,917
Important variables such as medications, comorbidities, measurement timing, and kidney function are absent.

148
00:16:32,917 --> 00:16:37,107
Those gaps are substantive limitations, not minor disclaimers.

149
00:16:37,107 --> 00:16:46,010
The prototype helps inspect a hypothesis; it does not diagnose, prescribe, triage symptoms, or claim regulatory approval.

150
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:53,451
The next step is not simply adding more visual features.

151
00:16:53,451 --> 00:17:00,863
A credible development path starts with consented, well-characterized longitudinal data and a preregistered evaluation plan.

152
00:17:00,863 --> 00:17:06,792
We would examine measurement quality, missingness, calibration, and performance across relevant subgroups.

153
00:17:06,792 --> 00:17:14,204
We would compare against stronger temporal baselines and test whether the residual state adds value.

154
00:17:14,204 --> 00:17:19,639
Clinician review would help define appropriate uses and identify failure cases.

155
00:17:19,639 --> 00:17:28,039
Any investigation of intervention effects would need a causal design rather than assuming regression coefficients are causal.

156
00:17:28,039 --> 00:17:34,463
Secure ingestion, authentication, data governance, and deletion controls must precede real patient deployment.

157
00:17:34,463 --> 00:17:39,898
Live device synchronization could then make the update loop more automatic.

158
00:17:39,898 --> 00:17:42,863
Each of these is future work.

159
00:17:42,863 --> 00:17:51,263
The present submission delivers a transparent, reproducible starting point whose assumptions and limits can be challenged directly.

160
00:17:53,763 --> 00:18:03,185
To reproduce PulseTwin, create a Python environment, install the pinned dependencies, and start the FastAPI application using the README command.

161
00:18:03,185 --> 00:18:08,368
The dashboard and API documentation are served by the same process.

162
00:18:08,368 --> 00:18:21,559
Run the model tests and evaluation script to regenerate the evidence, and use the browser scripts with Chromium to check the original workflow and all ten new features.

163
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:31,453
This package is prepared for Team Gimites: Yashwanth M as team leader, with Kalashikam Vijay Krishna, Subiksha K, and Shakthi K.

164
00:18:31,453 --> 00:18:35,222
Their names come from the supplied registration screenshot.

165
00:18:35,222 --> 00:18:43,702
The institutional affiliation has not been supplied, and the required unlisted YouTube publication still requires an authorized account.

166
00:18:43,702 --> 00:18:46,057
No contest submission is claimed.

167
00:18:46,057 --> 00:18:55,009
The contribution is a working, inspectable research prototype whose observations, assumptions, results, and limitations can be reproduced and challenged.
